    "media:imagetext": "SMOKING IS NOT PERMITTED ON BOARD THIS AIRCRAFT.\nTO FASTEN:\nInsert metal tab into\nmetal buckle until is\nsnaps.\nTO ADJUST:\nPull end of belt until desired\nsecureness is obtained\nTO REMOVE:\nInsert fingers under\nbuckle flange and lift\nupward.\nPLEASE OBSERVE\n\"NO SMOKING\" SIGN\nIt is a Comair, Inc. policy to\nrequest that all passengers\nrefrain from smoking aboard\nthe aircraft. We thank you for\nyour cooperation in this\nmatter.\nSEAT TRAY — Must be up and stowed\naway for takeoff and landing.\nPLEASE FASTEN SEAT\nBELTS BEFORE TAKEOFF\nAND LANDING\nAt takeoff and landing, seat\nbelts should be fastened. At\nthese times, the \"Fasten Seat\nBelt\" sign will be lighted. In\nbumpy air, the sign will be\nlighted during flight. There is\nno cause for alarm but we ask\nthat you comply for a more\ncomfortable ride. When the\nsign is off, your belt may be\nreleased.\nHOW TO USE FIRE EXTINGUISHER\n1. Remove from clip.\n2. Depress thumb safety.\n3. Direct nozzle to base of flame.\n4. Squeeze handle to discharge.\nDO NOT REMOVE FROM AIRPLANE\nFEDERAL LAWS REQUIRE THIS CARD BE KEPT IN THE SEAT POCKET\nFOR PASSENGER INFORMATION",
    "media:imagetext_created": 1787974231,
